= Part XII — Troubleshooting
== XII.1 Login fails
Possible cause: Missing public Supabase configuration, invalid credentials, expired recovery session, or provider rejection. Diagnosis: Check /api/config/public, browser network response, Auth status, and the exact user-facing error; do not log passwords or tokens. Solution: Restore approved configuration or repeat the supported recovery flow; keep error messages generic enough to avoid account enumeration.
=== Kiswahili
Sababu: Missing public Supabase configuration, invalid credentials, expired recovery session, or provider rejection. Utambuzi: Check /api/config/public, browser network response, Auth status, and the exact user-facing error; do not log passwords or tokens. Suluhisho: Restore approved configuration or repeat the supported recovery flow; keep error messages generic enough to avoid account enumeration.
